---
import { getEntry, render } from "astro:content";
import { Picture } from "astro:assets";
import { historyPhoto } from "../data/gallery";

/**
 * The holding's own history - the text migrated from /o-nas/ on the current site: the
 * founding year, the switch from vegetables to flowers, the awards.
 *
 * It is now the body of `/o-nas/`, the same address it had on WordPress, so the page that
 * ranks for it keeps ranking. The heading level is a prop for that reason: `h1` where the
 * block is the page, `h2` where it is a section on another one.
 *
 * ## It used to be a dark block, and that is what changed in September 2026
 *
 * This was the one full-bleed `--green-deep` plate outside the home page, which made
 * `/o-nas/` the one dark page on a site whose every other subpage - `/kontakt/`, `/faq/`,
 * `/inspiracje/`, the four category pages, the privacy policy - is a single flat section on
 * `--paper`. The owners asked for it to be brought into line, and it is now ink on paper
 * like the rest. Alternating grounds remain a home page device only.
 *
 * It also closed a seam that could not be closed any other way. A dark plate has to be
 * parted from the `--ink` footer by a light section (tokens.css, at `--green-band`: the
 * join is 1.44:1 and the footer colour is not negotiable), and on a page that is one block
 * long there was nothing to part them with - so the page simply ran out into the footer.
 * **Do not repaint this block dark again** without answering that.
 *
 * The text is longer than the placeholder paragraph the prototype carried, so this column
 * simply runs taller than the photograph beside it; nothing is trimmed to make the two
 * match.
 *
 * ## The one photo caption on the site, and why it is not a reversal
 *
 * September 2026: the owners asked for this frame to be captioned "Na wystawie kwiatow
 * w Konskowoli", which is also how the repository learned that the photograph is **not** the
 * holding's own tunnel but its stand at a flower show - see `historyPhoto` in
 * src/data/gallery.ts.
 *
 * The owners had captions stripped from every plant entry earlier that month
 * (docs/inwentaryzacja.md, "Podpisy pod zdjeciami - usuniete"), and `caption` went out of the
 * schema with them. **This does not bring that back.** That decision was about the fourteen
 * one-sentence captions under the plant entries; the slideshow kept its `<figcaption>`
 * throughout, because there it carries the editorial description. This one names a place the
 * picture cannot state for itself, which no `alt` should be doing - and the `alt` deliberately
 * does not repeat it, a duplication `Compositions.astro` had to fix once already. Do not read
 * this as licence to put captions back under the plant entries.
 *
 * The wording is the owners' own, with one preposition added: they wrote "Wystawie kwiatow
 * w Konskowoli", a locative with nothing to govern it, which under a photograph reads as a
 * typo rather than as a caption. "Na" is the smallest change that makes it a sentence and
 * keeps every word they chose. It is on their list in docs/inwentaryzacja.md to confirm or
 * put back.
 */
interface Props {
  level?: 1 | 2;
}

const { level = 2 } = Astro.props;
const Heading = `h${level}` as "h1" | "h2";

const entry = await getEntry("pages", "historia");
if (!entry) {
  throw new Error("Missing src/content/pages/historia.md - the history section has no text.");
}
const { Content } = await render(entry);

/** The design brief here says "zdjecie archiwalne" and this frame is still contemporary, so
 *  the request stays on the list in docs/inwentaryzacja.md - but it is no longer urgent.
 *
 *  What it replaced, in September 2026, was a planting borrowed out of the `compositions`
 *  collection through `compositionPhoto()`. That photograph is also on `/inspiracje/`, and a
 *  page about the holding showing a picture that belongs to another page is the weaker
 *  answer; `historyPhoto` is a frame of the holding itself and of nothing else. The pinning
 *  is in src/data/gallery.ts with the rest of the photographs the design asks for by name. */
---

<section id="historia" class="history" aria-labelledby="historia-title">
  <div class="history__text">
    <p class="eyebrow history__eyebrow">{entry.data.label}</p>
    <Heading class="history__title" id="historia-title">{entry.data.title}</Heading>
    <div class="history__body copy">
      <Content />
    </div>
  </div>
  <figure class="history__figure">
    <Picture
      class="history__photo"
      src={historyPhoto.src}
      formats={["avif", "webp"]}
      fallbackFormat="jpg"
      widths={[640, 1280]}
      sizes="(min-width: 1200px) 560px, (min-width: 700px) 45vw, 90vw"
      width={640}
      height={427}
      alt={historyPhoto.alt}
      loading="lazy"
    />
    <figcaption class="history__caption">Na wystawie kwiatów w Końskowoli</figcaption>
  </figure>
</section>

<style>
  /* No ground and no colour of its own: the section stands on the body's --paper and inherits
     --ink, exactly like .contact, whose two-column layout this is. No --focus-ring override
     either - the default --green is 4.95:1 here, and it was only raised while this block was
     dark. No border-top: the nav bar draws the edge above it, as on .faq and .contact. */
  .history {
    padding: var(--pad-section-wide) var(--edge);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 300px), 1fr));
    gap: var(--gap-columns);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .history__text {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.1rem;
    justify-items: start;
  }

  /* The global .eyebrow carries the weight, the tracking, the uppercase and --ochre; only the
     step is local, and it is the 0.72rem .faq__eyebrow and .policy__eyebrow use. --ochre-lit
     went with the dark ground - it is the lit variant, for --green-deep and --ink only. */
  .history__eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
  }

  .history__title {
    font-size: var(--text-h2-wide);
    line-height: 1.06;
    max-width: 24ch;
  }

  /* No colour: the prose inherits --ink, like .policy__body. --green-body is a paragraph
     colour for the dark plates and has nothing to sit on here. */
  .history__body {
    max-width: 54ch;
  }

  /* The photograph starts level with the `h1`, not with the small uppercase line above it.
     The offset is **the overline's own row**, written as the two values it is made of rather
     than as a nudge: its line box (0.72rem at the inherited 1.68) plus the text column's gap
     (1.1rem). If either changes this sum moves with it, which a round number would not.

     One accepted consequence: when the two columns collapse into one, this margin adds to the
     grid's row gap, so on a narrow screen there is ~37px more air between the prose and the
     photograph than there was. That is the right direction to err in, and buying it back would
     cost a breakpoint - which this project does not have. */
  .history__figure {
    margin: 0;
    margin-block-start: calc(0.72rem * 1.68 + 1.1rem);
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.7rem;
  }

  /* The handoff's figcaption, drawn at last: 0.8rem in the grey that tokens.css reserves for
     exactly this job - "every uppercase label and every photo caption" - at 4.99:1 on --paper.
     It is the only photo caption on the site outside the slideshow; History.astro's header
     says why that is not a reversal of the September 2026 removal. */
  .history__caption {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--ink-grey);
    max-width: 46ch;
  }

  /* The 3:2 box the placeholder used to hold, with the border every photograph on a light
     ground has - the same one .entry__photo draws. */
  .history__photo {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 3 / 2;
    object-fit: cover;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
</style>
